Chapter: RecheckSubject
  grounds Device.Port

 The mutation corpus subject. Deliberately exercises exactly the forms
 the rechecker examines: a sum with two constructors of different payload
 types, a match that takes both apart, bounded-integer signatures, a
 linear parameter, and an effectful function reached from the entry
 point.

 Payload types differ between the two constructors on purpose. A subject
 whose constructors both carried Integer could not distinguish a
 sub-pattern bound at the wrong field type from one bound correctly,
 which is the property those mutations are aimed at.

Section: Definitions

  Shade =
   | Dim (Integer)
   | Bright (Text)

 A second sum exists so the corpus can plant a constructor that resolves
 as a name but does not belong to the sum its reference is typed to build.
 With one sum type that mutation is indistinguishable from an unbound
 name, and it was: the arm meant to catch it never ran.

  Weather =
   | Fair (Integer)
   | Foul (Text)

  narrow : Integer between 0 and 10 -> Integer between 0 and 20
  narrow (n) = n * 2

  shade-of : Shade -> Text
  shade-of (s) =
   when s
    is Dim (k) -> show k
    is Bright (t) -> t

  weather-of : Weather -> Text
  weather-of (v) =
   when v
    is Fair (k) -> show k
    is Foul (t) -> t

  label : Integer -> Text
  label (n) = show n & "!"

  consume-once : linear Integer -> Integer
  consume-once (q) = q + 1

 touch performs port-out-byte, a [Device.Port] intrinsic, while its own
 signature is pure. That is legal ONLY because this chapter grounds
 Device.Port, so the mutation that deletes the grounds entry from the
 wire must come back DISAGREE. Without a grounded def here, the check
 that consults the table could be deleted outright and the corpus would
 not notice.

  touch : Integer -> Integer
  touch (p) =
   let w = port-out-byte p 0
   in w

 Everything must be reachable from the entry point or the IR prunes it,
 so the effectful arm is called rather than merely defined.

  announce : Text -> [Console] Nothing
  announce (m) = print-line-uni m

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   announce (shade-of (Bright "hi") & shade-of (Dim 3) & label (narrow 5) & weather-of (Fair 1) & show (consume-once 9) & show (touch 128))
  end

